{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794344790,"nonce":"YMXrWw7NVB1GvYT2VPbRDFFCBjk=","message":"Cause found with BLINC_MOTION_TRACE on fs-people (Release, kwin virtual): in the 60 frames per second phases every frame has all ask terms false and another_frame false (cursor, animation, scroll, overlay, css, flow, scheduler, none asks), did_rebuild false, drawn true, p4 0.2 to 3.4 ms. The frames come only from the Wayland keep-alive: present.rs requests the next redraw after every present when ws.wayland_keep_alive is set (lifecycle.rs, true on any Wayland window), and winit delivers it on the compositor's next frame callback. Not the cursor blink (a focused field with nothing else asks only for a 400 ms wake, 2 commits a second), not an animation, not a never-cleared dirty flag. In this nested kwin the compositor stopped delivering frame callbacks to the idle surface after about 10 s, after which commits fell to 1 to 2 a second; on a compositor that keeps delivering them the idle window stays at 60 a second. Removing the keep-alive is what the code comments say starves the swapchain, so it is a design question for the maintainer, not a small fix: re-present the cached frame instead of running the render phase, or keep-alive only for a short time after the last frame that drew something. No change made.","files":null}]}